{
 "source": "geneva",
 "book": "PRO",
 "chapter": 24,
 "units": [
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.7",
   "range": "PRO.24.7",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "a24a260f",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.7#p1-a24a260f",
     "text": "In the place where wisdom should be shown.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "gate"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.10",
   "range": "PRO.24.10",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4aba1808",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.10#p1-4aba1808",
     "text": "Man has no trial of his strength till he is in trouble.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "faintest in the day of adversity"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.11",
   "range": "PRO.24.11",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "1ce16c56",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.11#p1-1ce16c56",
     "text": "No one can be excused, if he does not help the innocent when he is in danger.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "death"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.13",
   "range": "PRO.24.13",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "4e623206",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.13#p1-4e623206",
     "text": "As honey is sweet and pleasant to the taste, so wisdom is to the soul.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "honey"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.16",
   "range": "PRO.24.16",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6e9bf39b",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.16#p1-6e9bf39b",
     "text": "He is subject to many perils, but God delivers him.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "falleth seven times"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.18",
   "range": "PRO.24.18",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "3f4c02b7",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.18#p1-3f4c02b7",
     "text": "To be avenged on you.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "from him"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.22",
   "range": "PRO.24.22",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "dd692faf",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.22#p1-dd692faf",
     "text": "Meaning, either of the wicked and seditious, as in Pr 24:19,21 or of them who do not fear God or obey their king.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "both",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Pr 24:19,21",
       "ref": "PRO.24.19"
      },
      {
       "text": "Pr 24:19,21",
       "ref": "PRO.24.21"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.27",
   "range": "PRO.24.27",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e8938f84",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.27#p1-e8938f84",
     "text": "Be sure of the means how to compass it, before you take any enterprise in hand.",
     "label": "h",
     "anchor": "and afterwards build thy house"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.29",
   "range": "PRO.24.29",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "38ff02cd",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.29#p1-38ff02cd",
     "text": "He shows what is the nature of the wicked, to revenge wrong for wrong.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "will render to the man according"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.32",
   "range": "PRO.24.32",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "52e8b12c",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.32#p1-52e8b12c",
     "text": "That I might learn by another man's fault.",
     "label": "k",
     "anchor": "instruction"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/PRO.24.33",
   "range": "PRO.24.33",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "40e8e4bb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/PRO.24.33#p1-40e8e4bb",
     "text": "Read Geneva \"Pr 6:10\"",
     "label": "l",
     "anchor": "a little slumber"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
